    "type": "scenario",
    "front": "SCENARIO: PR review workflow: every PR must be reviewed for code style, security vulnerabilities, AND documentation accuracy. Which architectural pattern?",
    "back": "✅ PROMPT CHAINING: separate sequential passes, each with a distinct focus.\n1. Style pass: only evaluate code formatting and conventions\n2. Security pass: only look for vulnerability patterns\n3. Documentation pass: only verify accuracy of comments and docs\nMerge outputs into final synthesis.\n\n❌ Dynamic subagent decomposition (the workflow is predictable and ALWAYS the same)\n❌ A routing agent (all 3 aspects are needed for EVERY PR, not just one)\n❌ Single massive prompt covering all 3 simultaneously (attention dilution across concerns)\n\n💡 When workflow is highly predictable and mandatory: prompt chaining.\n💡 Isolating distinct cognitive lenses prevents cross-contamination.",
