    "front": "SCENARIO: You're restructuring a monolith into 40+ microservices — changes across dozens of files, decisions about service boundaries and module dependencies. Best approach?",
    "back": "✅ PLAN MODE: Explore codebase, understand dependencies, design approach BEFORE making changes.\n→ Safe exploration + architectural design with zero side effects\n→ User reviews and approves the plan before any changes happen\n→ Then direct execution for the approved implementation\n\n❌ Start with direct execution and make incremental changes\n   (risks costly rework when dependency conflicts discovered late)\n❌ Direct execution with comprehensive upfront instructions\n   (assumes you know the structure without exploring it first)\n\n💡 Large-scale + architectural decisions → plan mode first, always.\n💡 The cost of a planning pass is trivial vs. the cost of reversing wrong changes.",
