    "front": "SCENARIO: SLA requires results within 30 hours. Batch API takes up to 24h. Which submission frequency meets SLA while maximizing cost efficiency?",
    "back": "✅ Every 6 HOURS — the maximum interval that still satisfies the SLA.\n\nMath: batch_interval + 24h ≤ 30h → interval ≤ 6h\n6h = fewest submissions = lowest overhead = maximum cost efficiency.\nIt sits precisely on the optimal boundary.\n\n❌ Every 4h: meets SLA but submits more batches than necessary (extra overhead)\n❌ Once daily: 24 + 24 = 48h → FAILS the 30h SLA\n❌ Sync API: loses 50% cost savings\n\n⚠️ Exam asks for MAX COST EFFICIENCY → 6h is correct (on the boundary)\n⚠️ Production reality: use 4h buffer. Exam: 6h.",
